1
00:00:01,921 --> 00:00:03,298
Hoo, hoo!

2
00:00:03,410 --> 00:00:04,337
Hi!

3
00:00:04,387 --> 00:00:06,414
It's me, Popcorn!

4
00:00:06,536 --> 00:00:11,767
Welcome to Popcorn Tales, the
cozy nest of bedtime stories.

5
00:00:12,079 --> 00:00:15,508
Hug your teddy, because
tonight's story is:

6
00:00:15,558 --> 00:00:17,872
The Shoemaker and the Elves!

7
00:00:22,457 --> 00:00:27,921
Once upon a time, in an old town
covered in snow, there lived a shoemaker

8
00:00:27,971 --> 00:00:32,963
named Otto, with his wife,
Clara, in a simple house,

9
00:00:33,013 --> 00:00:35,246
with the workshop downstairs.

10
00:00:35,876 --> 00:00:40,762
Otto was very honest and worked with
great care, but times were hard,

11
00:00:40,820 --> 00:00:43,484
and he was growing poorer and poorer.

12
00:00:43,625 --> 00:00:48,034
One day, he realized that he only had
enough leather for one more pair of

13
00:00:48,084 --> 00:00:51,900
shoes, and not a single
coin to buy any more.

14
00:00:52,556 --> 00:00:57,297
That night, he cut the leather very
carefully, left the pieces on the

15
00:00:57,347 --> 00:01:01,914
workbench, and decided to sew
everything the next morning.

16
00:01:02,504 --> 00:01:06,481
Early tomorrow I will finish this pair
of shoes, and then we'll see what we

17
00:01:06,531 --> 00:01:07,368
can do,

18
00:01:07,418 --> 00:01:10,082
Otto said, blowing out the candle.

19
00:01:10,686 --> 00:01:12,062
Hoo, hoo!

20
00:01:12,187 --> 00:01:14,280
It's so cold out here!

21
00:01:14,397 --> 00:01:19,826
The shoemaker is so kind and so
hard-working, I really wish I could help,

22
00:01:19,876 --> 00:01:23,359
Popcorn said, shivering on the windowsill.

23
00:01:24,421 --> 00:01:28,982
The next morning, Otto came down to the
workshop and could hardly believe his

24
00:01:29,032 --> 00:01:30,232
eyes.

25
00:01:32,952 --> 00:01:37,263
On the workbench, instead of the pieces
of leather, there was a finished pair

26
00:01:37,313 --> 00:01:42,352
of shoes, so beautifully sewn that
not a single stitch was crooked.

27
00:01:42,927 --> 00:01:45,841
Clara, come and see this, quickly!

28
00:01:46,003 --> 00:01:48,573
Somebody made the shoes during the night!

29
00:01:48,623 --> 00:01:51,592
Otto called, straightening his glasses.

30
00:01:52,208 --> 00:01:56,158
Clara came down the stairs,
looked closely at the shoes,

31
00:01:56,208 --> 00:01:58,497
and clapped her hands with joy.

32
00:01:59,069 --> 00:02:01,507
What lovely shoes, Otto!

33
00:02:01,739 --> 00:02:04,227
They look as if they were made for a king,

34
00:02:04,277 --> 00:02:06,454
Clara said, amazed.

35
00:02:07,549 --> 00:02:12,568
A little later, an elegant customer in
a top hat and a long coat came into the

36
00:02:12,618 --> 00:02:16,088
workshop, stamping the snow off his boots.

37
00:02:17,865 --> 00:02:21,649
He tried on the new shoes, took
a few steps around the workshop,

38
00:02:21,699 --> 00:02:24,418
and broke into an enormous smile.

39
00:02:24,991 --> 00:02:28,656
I have never worn such comfortable
shoes in my whole life!

40
00:02:28,944 --> 00:02:31,562
I insist on paying twice the price,

41
00:02:31,612 --> 00:02:34,401
the customer said, handing over the coins.

42
00:02:35,005 --> 00:02:39,483
With that money, Otto bought enough
leather for two pairs of shoes,

43
00:02:39,533 --> 00:02:43,919
and that night he cut it all and
left the pieces on the workbench.

44
00:02:44,550 --> 00:02:48,681
In the morning, both pairs were ready,
and they were sold that very day;

45
00:02:48,731 --> 00:02:52,945
and the next day there was leather for
four pairs, and all four were ready as

46
00:02:52,995 --> 00:02:54,195
well.

47
00:02:54,393 --> 00:02:55,769
Hoo, hoo!

48
00:02:55,878 --> 00:03:01,075
Somebody is secretly working in this
workshop, and I am very curious to find

49
00:03:01,125 --> 00:03:02,404
out who it is,

50
00:03:02,454 --> 00:03:04,951
Popcorn said, from the shop sign.

51
00:03:06,052 --> 00:03:10,627
And so it went on for many weeks, and
the workshop became famous all over

52
00:03:10,677 --> 00:03:14,952
town, and Otto and Clara
never went without again.

53
00:03:15,602 --> 00:03:20,433
The lady from the bakery came to buy
shoes, and so did the school teacher,

54
00:03:20,561 --> 00:03:25,316
the mailman who walked all day long,
and even the mayor of the town,

55
00:03:25,366 --> 00:03:27,433
with his cane and his hat.

56
00:03:28,058 --> 00:03:30,231
And they all said the same thing:

57
00:03:30,281 --> 00:03:35,306
that those were the softest and most
beautiful shoes they had ever worn.

58
00:03:35,948 --> 00:03:40,737
One December night, just before
Christmas, Otto had an idea.

59
00:03:41,293 --> 00:03:45,604
Clara, how about we stay awake tonight,
to see who it is that helps us so

60
00:03:45,654 --> 00:03:46,407
much?

61
00:03:46,457 --> 00:03:49,134
Otto asked, speaking very slowly.

62
00:03:49,702 --> 00:03:51,298
What a good idea!

63
00:03:51,491 --> 00:03:56,078
Let's leave a candle burning and hide
behind the coats hanging on the rack,

64
00:03:56,128 --> 00:04:00,347
Clara answered, sounding
very excited about that idea.

65
00:04:00,963 --> 00:04:04,788
The two of them cut the leather,
left the pieces on the workbench,

66
00:04:04,838 --> 00:04:08,890
and hid behind the coats,
as quiet as two mice.

67
00:04:09,029 --> 00:04:13,174
When the clock struck midnight,
the door opened without a sound,

68
00:04:13,224 --> 00:04:17,721
and in came two tiny elves,
no bigger than a boot.

69
00:04:24,525 --> 00:04:30,170
They had pointy ears, messy hair and
rosy cheeks, but they were wearing old,

70
00:04:30,220 --> 00:04:33,883
torn clothes, and they walked
barefoot through the snow.

71
00:04:34,519 --> 00:04:38,677
The two of them climbed onto the
workbench, picked up the pieces of leather,

72
00:04:38,727 --> 00:04:43,794
and began to sew and hammer so quickly
that their hands seemed to fly.

73
00:04:45,483 --> 00:04:49,038
One more stitch here, one more nail
there, and this shoe will be perfect for

74
00:04:49,088 --> 00:04:50,472
the lady from the bakery,

75
00:04:50,522 --> 00:04:53,214
one of the elves said, smiling.

76
00:04:53,870 --> 00:04:58,140
Before the rooster crowed, all the
shoes were finished and lined up on the

77
00:04:58,190 --> 00:05:01,604
workbench, and the elves
ran out through the door.

78
00:05:04,596 --> 00:05:08,621
In the morning, Clara could not
stop thinking about the elves.

79
00:05:09,246 --> 00:05:13,734
Otto, the elves have helped us so
much, and they go around in the cold,

80
00:05:13,784 --> 00:05:16,385
in torn clothes and with no shoes.

81
00:05:16,667 --> 00:05:19,056
Let's make them a Christmas present,

82
00:05:19,106 --> 00:05:22,242
Clara said, with shining eyes.

83
00:05:22,795 --> 00:05:25,486
What a wonderful idea, Clara!

84
00:05:25,605 --> 00:05:29,564
You make the clothes, and I'll
make two pairs of tiny shoes,

85
00:05:29,614 --> 00:05:34,001
Otto answered, already picking up
the softest leather in the workshop.

86
00:05:34,628 --> 00:05:38,953
Clara sewed two green shirts,
two brown pairs of trousers,

87
00:05:39,003 --> 00:05:42,626
two red waistcoats, and
two warm woolly hats.

88
00:05:44,430 --> 00:05:50,130
And Otto made two pairs of tiny shoes,
with the same care he had learned from

89
00:05:50,180 --> 00:05:51,608
watching the elves.

90
00:05:52,193 --> 00:05:53,570
Hoo, hoo!

91
00:05:53,673 --> 00:05:55,714
What a beautiful present!

92
00:05:55,876 --> 00:06:00,415
Making something with your own hands
is a lovely way to say thank you,

93
00:06:00,465 --> 00:06:02,796
Popcorn said, very moved.

94
00:06:03,873 --> 00:06:09,517
On Christmas Eve, instead of leather,
Otto and Clara left the new clothes and

95
00:06:09,567 --> 00:06:13,953
shoes on the workbench, and hid
behind the coats once again.

96
00:06:14,575 --> 00:06:18,392
At midnight, the elves came
in and looked for the leather,

97
00:06:18,450 --> 00:06:22,628
but they found the clothes,
the hats and the shoes instead.

98
00:06:26,234 --> 00:06:29,573
They were so happy that they
put everything on in a hurry,

99
00:06:29,623 --> 00:06:34,198
and began to dance and jump on the
workbench, over the chairs and over the

100
00:06:34,248 --> 00:06:35,448
stools.

101
00:06:35,887 --> 00:06:37,810
Look how smart we are now!

102
00:06:37,931 --> 00:06:40,155
We don't need to be shoemakers any more,

103
00:06:40,205 --> 00:06:43,827
the other elf said, laughing
and spinning around.

104
00:06:44,473 --> 00:06:49,595
The two of them danced all the way to
the door, gave one last happy jump,

105
00:06:49,667 --> 00:06:52,831
and went off into the
snow, humming with joy.

106
00:06:56,192 --> 00:07:00,989
The elves never came back, but Otto's
workshop stayed full of customers,

107
00:07:01,039 --> 00:07:04,828
because he had learned to sew
with all the care in the world.

108
00:07:05,437 --> 00:07:10,123
Otto and Clara lived happily,
and every year, on Christmas Eve,

109
00:07:10,173 --> 00:07:14,178
they left a plate of cookies and two
mugs of warm milk on the workbench,

110
00:07:14,228 --> 00:07:15,531
just in case.

111
00:07:16,158 --> 00:07:20,830
Sometimes, on snowy nights, Otto looked
out of the window and thought he could

112
00:07:20,880 --> 00:07:26,238
hear, far away, two little
voices laughing and dancing.

113
00:07:26,827 --> 00:07:28,204
Hoo, hoo!

114
00:07:28,309 --> 00:07:34,027
When someone helps us, we say thank you,
and gratitude is even more beautiful

115
00:07:34,077 --> 00:07:36,415
when we give something back with love,

116
00:07:36,465 --> 00:07:39,837
Popcorn said, blinking her big eyes.

117
00:07:47,142 --> 00:07:48,342
The End.

118
00:07:50,057 --> 00:07:50,769
Hoo...

119
00:07:50,819 --> 00:07:51,843
Psst!

120
00:07:51,893 --> 00:07:53,465
Are you still awake?

121
00:07:53,618 --> 00:07:55,671
Did you like tonight's story?

122
00:07:55,808 --> 00:08:00,667
Otto and Clara showed us that when
someone helps us we should say thank you,

123
00:08:00,717 --> 00:08:04,898
and that gratitude is even more beautiful
when we give something back with

124
00:08:04,948 --> 00:08:06,068
love.

125
00:08:06,118 --> 00:08:10,424
Good night, sleep tight, and
have the sweetest dreams.

126
00:08:10,720 --> 00:08:15,618
Grown-ups: if you enjoyed it,
please subscribe to Popcorn Tales,

127
00:08:15,668 --> 00:08:18,073
for more stories at bedtime.

128
00:08:18,377 --> 00:08:19,577
Hoo...

